relationships:
Grandson of Charles II (FRS 1665); 
Son of Charles Lennox, 1st Duke of Richmond and Lennox, and his wife, Anne, widow of Henry Belasyde, 2nd Baron Belasyde of Warlaby, and daughter of Francis Brudenell, Lord Brudenell, and his wife, Frances, daughter of James Savile, Earl of Sussex; succeeded his father (1723); at the age of 18, married Sarah, 13-year-old daughter of William Cadogan, 1st Earl Cadogan, and his wife, Margaret Cecilia, daughter of John or William Munter, Councillor of the Court of Holland, to cancel a gaming debt between their parents; succeeded to the Dukedom of Aubigny in France on the death of his paternal grandmother, Louise de Keroualle, Duchess of Portsmouth (1734); 
father of Charles Lennox, 3rd Duke of Richmond and Lennox (FRS 1755)

